@startuml cls-notification-configuration
title Class Diagram — Notification & Configuration

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class AcademicActor <<external — academic>> {
}
class School <<external — academic>> {
}

enum Severity <<enumeration>> {
  INFO
  WARNING
  CRITICAL
}

enum Channel <<enumeration>> {
  DASHBOARD
  EMAIL
  PUSH
}

class AlertType {
  +alertTypeId: Int
  +code: String
  +name: String
  +severity: Severity
  +channel: Channel
}

class Alert {
  +alertId: Long
  +academicActorId: Long
  +alertTypeId: Int
  +raisedAt: DateTime
  +resolvedAt: DateTime
  +raise()
  +resolve()
}

class AcademicConfiguration {
  +configurationId: Int
  +schoolId: Int
  +configurationName: String
  +configurationValue: String
  +description: String
}

class SecurityConfiguration {
  +configurationId: Int
  +configurationName: String
  +configurationValue: String
  +description: String
}

AlertType "1" -- "0..*" Alert : alert.alert_type_id FK
Alert --> Severity
AlertType --> Channel

Alert ..> AcademicActor : academic_actor_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
AcademicConfiguration ..> School : school_id\n(cross-context, no FK)

note right of Alert
  RN-42: alerts are system-generated for
  defined event types. RN-43: resolution
  requires the appropriate permission.
  resolvedAt NULL = unresolved. No code raises
  channel=EMAIL alerts today — only the
  password-recovery e-mail flow sends mail
  (see c1-system-context.mmd).
end note

note bottom of AcademicConfiguration
  Scoped per school (uq_academic_configuration
  on school_id + configuration_name), e.g.
  tardy_tolerance_minutes.
end note

note bottom of SecurityConfiguration
  Global (no school_id), uq on
  configuration_name, e.g. max_login_attempts,
  session_timeout_minutes,
  lockout_duration_minutes. Password policy
  lives in identity.password_policy, not here.
end note

note as N1
  All classes also carry the standard audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted
  here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and
  06-data/domains/07-notification.md /
  08-configuration.md for the column-level ER
  view.
end note

@enduml
